// Hamilton County, Ohio — curated directory of meaningful links.
// Single source of truth for the app. Keep entries verified and current.
// Fields: name, category, subcategory, url, description
// Last reviewed: 2026-11-09
//
// Every URL below was fetched and its content checked against the organization
// it claims to be. Sites that block automated fetching (the Cincinnati Enquirer,
// WLWT and CET) were checked in a browser.
//
// THINGS THAT CHANGED SINCE JULY
//
//   * County animal control is contracted to Cincinnati Animal CARE (not SPCA
//     Cincinnati, which is a separate shelter).
//   * The county solid waste district is now Hamilton County ReSource.
//   * JFS, Public Health, DD Services, Veterans Services, ReSource and the Air
//     Quality Agency moved to the Central Campus, 1701 Patricia McCollum Way.
//   * norwood-ohio.com is a stale 2010-era site; Norwood is now norwoodohio.gov.
//   * Silverton is a village again; St. Bernard's own site calls it a village.
//   * The Minority Business Accelerator is now the Cincinnati Business Excellerator.
//   * Coney Island closed permanently after 2023; Shriners Cincinnati moved to
//     Dayton; Cincinnati Christian University closed in 2019.
//   * The Auditor's property search is wEdge by DEVNET, Inc.
//
// TRAPS
//
//   The CITY of Hamilton, Ohio is in Butler County. Hamilton County TN
//   (Chattanooga), IN, NY. Northern Kentucky institutions and attractions
//   (Newport Aquarium, Ark Encounter, NKU, St. Elizabeth). Kings Island (Warren)
//   and the Cincinnati Nature Center (Clermont). harrison-chamber.com is Harrison,
//   Arkansas.
//
// GEOGRAPHY
//
//   * Cincinnati (seat) plus 17 other cities, 19 villages and 12 townships, each
//     with its home page. Loveland spans Hamilton, Clermont and Warren; Milford is
//     mostly Clermont; Sharonville is partly Butler. Fairfield's sliver is left to
//     Butler County.
//   * Twenty-two public school districts; Great Oaks' Diamond Oaks and Scarlet
//     Oaks campuses are in the county.
//   * The Port and the Hamilton County Landbank share 221 E. Fourth Street; the
//     First District Court of Appeals serves Hamilton County only.
//
// LEFT OUT
//
//   * Some FQHCs (Crossroad, WinMed, HealthCare Connection), private schools and
//     smaller news outlets (Business Courier, Cincinnati Herald, Signal
//     Cincinnati) were not reached in this pass.

